WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.499 --> 00:00:15.719
RAE: I'll be very brief. Thanks, Miroslav. 

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:18.529
And good to see you all across the globe, there. 

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:21.800
Let me start with

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.619
a distinction

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:27.189
not very different from thick versus thin 

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:31.829
that comes from the psychologist and philosopher William James, 

00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:32.929
who distinguished

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:34.489
acute

00:00:34.489 --> 00:00:36.420
and chronic religion.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.570
Acute religion is

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.100
identity-defining

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.800
and demands

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.700
to subordinate other forms of knowledge

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.720
to religious doctrine or dogma.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.680
And chronic religion is

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:55.790
more porous and more--

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.140
penetrable

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.780
by other ideas.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.300
The thought

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.540
I have is that acute religion, combined with certain

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.840
external circumstances,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.490
is the most dangerous combination. And those external circumstances

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.640
would be poverty;

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.750
isolation;

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.149
government which is

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:22.880
undemocratic

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.220
and authoritarian,

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.330
or wholly inept

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.590
as in failed states;

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:32.990
illiteracy;

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:37.730
and early stages in the world demographic transition--

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.780
that is, stages where you have

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:44.200
disproportionately large numbers of young people

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.370
in a population

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:51.200
and low expectations of life span.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.970
If you look at

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:57.740
violence which is not institutionally organized,

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:02.500
the vast majority of it comes from very young men.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:09.500
and that combination is-- is, I think, particularly dangerous.

00:02:09.519 --> 00:02:13.719
I teach in the business school,

00:02:13.719 --> 00:02:20.469
and I therefore like to believe that commerce is a good thing.

00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:21.889
Voltaire,

00:02:21.889 --> 00:02:23.590
centuries ago,

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.549
put forward the proposition that

00:02:27.549 --> 00:02:28.609
Mohammadens,

00:02:28.609 --> 00:02:30.099
Jews

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:30.720
Christians,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.159
and Hindus

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:35.549
who meet in a stock exchange

00:02:35.549 --> 00:02:40.579
learn to tolerate one another and learn to have a certain sense of ironic detachment

00:02:40.579 --> 00:02:44.249
about their religious differences.

00:02:44.249 --> 00:02:47.909
And I think actually the process of globalization

00:02:47.909 --> 00:02:51.539
has within it the potential to promote

00:02:51.539 --> 00:02:53.670
this more ironic,

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.169
chronic

00:02:55.169 --> 00:02:56.549
attitude toward

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:58.219
religious

00:02:58.219 --> 00:02:58.770
dogma

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.590
and i'll stop there.

